{"step_index":9335,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-26T07:03:41Z","thinking":"The agent identifies potentially dangerous commands related to file deletion and modification that are explicitly checked before execution. These include commands that use `find` to delete files, shell expansions invoking `rm`, and several commands used in git for cleaning and resetting the repository. Additional checks for commands manipulating the file system directly (e.g. `>` to protected paths and using `chattr -i`) and standard library functions for deletion will be performed. These checks will prevent unintended data loss or modifications.\n\n\nThe analysis reveals numerous file deletion/truncation methods bypassing the current protection. Several common utilities like `shred`, `dd`, `cp`, and various scripting language's file manipulation functions are not explicitly guarded. Direct system calls and redirection to `/dev/null` similarly offer unmonitored file modification pathways.\n\n\nSeveral methods using scripting, dynamic attribute lookup and external utilities like `git rm`, `tar --remove-files`, and `zip -m` directly facilitate deletion and are not caught by existing safeguards. Base64 and hex encoded shell commands also bypass the current checks because of how `delete_guard.py` is configured. Direct system calls and compiled binaries present another attack vector.\n\n\nA Python script will be constructed to systematically test each deletion command's effectiveness against the existing protection mechanism. The script will create test files, simulate execution, and verify if the file is successfully deleted, truncated, or remains untouched based on the `delete_guard.py` hook's response. The responses will be recorded. The results, indicating blocked commands and successful deletions, will provide a clear understanding of the existing protection's effectiveness.\n\n\nTesting must include actual execution to verify allowed deletions. A comprehensive suite of 50 commands will systematically test the protection mechanism, covering multiple deletion methods. All test files will reside in a dedicated, isolated directory, ensuring no interference with project code.\n\nThe 50 commands were categorized into direct standard Unix deletion and standard Python deletion functions to guide testing and expected results. The test will record the hook's responses, including success/failure and bypass information.\n\n\nThe planned tests expand to incorporate commands from categories like Python standard library functions, Git utilities, and truncation tools, with an expectation the protections will block certain commands. Alternative Unix utilities, representing a potential bypass, are also included. The Python script will now execute these commands and observe the `delete_guard.py` hook's response.\n\n\nThe provided list of commands offers a thorough test suite for evaluating potential bypasses, categorized into protected and bypass methods. The initial 29 commands should be handled by current rules, while the remaining 21 expose vulnerabilities. These encompass scripting, dynamic calls, obfuscation, and direct system calls.\n\nA Python script will be implemented to sequentially execute each command within an isolated testing environment. This allows for observing the behavior of the `delete_guard.py` hook. The output will explicitly identify successful deletions and highlight bypassed protections.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"CodeContent":"#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"\n50-Command Deletion Benchmark Test\nAuthor: Antigravity AI (Pair Programming with Iraq Bhai)\nTarget: Azure VM 'FatehAli'\nObjective: Test 50 diverse deletion methods against delete_guard.py and the OS/kernel.\n\"\"\"\n\nimport os\nimport sys\nimport subprocess\nimport shutil\n\n# Import delete_guard's inspect_command to see hook verdict\nsys.path.insert(0, \"/home/azureuser/AGY-MASTER/POLICIES\")\nfrom delete_guard import inspect_command\n\nTEST_DIR = \"/tmp/test_50_del\"\nshutil.rmtree(TEST_DIR, ignore_errors=True)\nos.makedirs(TEST_DIR, exist_ok=True)\n\n# Prepare 50 test cases: (id, name, command_string, setup_func, target_file, expected_target_type)\n# target_type: 'file', 'dir', 'file_empty'\n\ntests = []\n\ndef add_test(test_id, name, category, cmd, target_rel, is_dir=False, is_gz=False):\n    tests.append({\n        \"id\": test_id,\n        \"name\": name,\n        \"category\": category,\n        \"cmd\": cmd,\n        \"target\": os.path.join(TEST_DIR, target_rel),\n        \"is_dir\": is_dir,\n        \"is_gz\": is_gz\n    })\n\n# --- Category 1: Direct Standard Unix Deletion (Rules 1, 2, 4, 5) ---\nadd_test(1, \"Standard rm\", \"Unix Standard\", \"rm /tmp/test_50_del/f1.txt\", \"f1.txt\")\nadd_test(2, \"Absolute /bin/rm\", \"Unix Standard\", \"/bin/rm /tmp/test_50_del/f2.txt\", \"f2.txt\")\nadd_test(3, \"Absolute /usr/bin/rm -f\", \"Unix Standard\", \"/usr/bin/rm -f /tmp/test_50_del/f3.txt\", \"f3.txt\")\nadd_test(4, \"Standard unlink\", \"Unix Standard\", \"unlink /tmp/test_50_del/f4.txt\", \"f4.txt\")\nadd_test(5, \"Absolute /usr/bin/unlink\", \"Unix Standard\", \"/usr/bin/unlink /tmp/test_50_del/f5.txt\", \"f5.txt\")\nadd_test(6, \"Standard rmdir\", \"Unix Standard\", \"rmdir /tmp/test_50_del/d6\", \"d6\", is_dir=True)\nadd_test(7, \"Absolute /bin/rmdir\", \"Unix Standard\", \"/bin/rmdir /tmp/test_50_del/d7\", \"d7\", is_dir=True)\nadd_test(8, \"find -delete\", \"Unix Standard\", \"find /tmp/test_50_del -name f8.txt -delete\", \"f8.txt\")\nadd_test(9, \"find -exec rm\", \"Unix Standard\", \"find /tmp/test_50_del -name f9.txt -exec rm {} \\\\;\", \"f9.txt\")\nadd_test(10, \"find -exec /bin/rm\", \"Unix Standard\", \"find /tmp/test_50_del -name f10.txt -exec /bin/rm {} \\\\;\", \"f10.txt\")\nadd_test(11, \"xargs rm\", \"Unix Standard\", \"echo /tmp/test_50_del/f11.txt | xargs rm\", \"f11.txt\")\nadd_test(12, \"bash -c 'rm ...'\", \"Unix Wrapper\", \"bash -c 'rm /tmp/test_50_del/f12.txt'\", \"f12.txt\")\nadd_test(13, \"sh -c 'rm ...'\", \"Unix Wrapper\", \"sh -c 'rm /tmp/test_50_del/f13.txt'\", \"f13.txt\")\nadd_test(14, \"eval 'rm ...'\", \"Unix Wrapper\", \"eval 'rm /tmp/test_50_del/f14.txt'\", \"f14.txt\")\nadd_test(15, \"$(echo rm) ...\", \"Unix Subst\", \"$(echo rm) /tmp/test_50_del/f15.txt\", \"f15.txt\")\n\n# --- Category 2: Python Deletion APIs (Rule 3) ---\nadd_test(16, \"Python os.remove()\", \"Python API\", \"python3 -c \\\"import os; os.remove('/tmp/test_50_del/f16.txt')\\\"\", \"f16.txt\")\nadd_test(17, \"Python os.unlink()\", \"Python API\", \"python3 -c \\\"import os; os.unlink('/tmp/test_50_del/f17.txt')\\\"\", \"f17.txt\")\nadd_test(18, \"Python os.rmdir()\", \"Python API\", \"python3 -c \\\"import os; os.rmdir('/tmp/test_50_del/d18')\\\"\", \"d18\", is_dir=True)\nadd_test(19, \"Python shutil.rmtree()\", \"Python API\", \"python3 -c \\\"import shutil; shutil.rmtree('/tmp/test_50_del/d19')\\\"\", \"d19\", is_dir=True)\nadd_test(20, \"Python Path.unlink()\", \"Python API\", \"python3 -c \\\"from pathlib import Path; Path('/tmp/test_50_del/f20.txt').unlink()\\\"\", \"f20.txt\")\nadd_test(21, \"Python Path.rmdir()\", \"Python API\", \"python3 -c \\\"from pathlib import Path; Path('/tmp/test_50_del/d21').rmdir()\\\"\", \"d21\", is_dir=True)\n\n# --- Category 3: Git & Truncation Guardrails (Rules 9, 10, 11, 12, 13, 23, 26) ---\nadd_test(22, \"git clean -f\", \"Git Guard\", \"git clean -fd\", \"f22.txt\")\nadd_test(23, \"git reset --hard\", \"Git Guard\", \"git reset --hard HEAD\", \"f23.txt\")\nadd_test(24, \"git checkout --\", \"Git Guard\", \"git checkout -- f24.txt\", \"f24.txt\")\nadd_test(25, \"git restore\", \"Git Guard\", \"git restore f25.txt\", \"f25.txt\")\nadd_test(26, \"rsync --delete\", \"Sync Guard\", \"rsync -av --delete /tmp/empty/ /tmp/test_50_del/d26/\", \"d26\", is_dir=True)\nadd_test(27, \"truncate -s 0\", \"Truncate Guard\", \"truncate -s 0 /tmp/test_50_del/f27.txt\", \"f27.txt\")\nadd_test(28, \"fallocate -l 0\", \"Truncate Guard\", \"fallocate -l 0 /tmp/test_50_del/f28.txt\", \"f28.txt\")\nadd_test(29, \"sudo rm\", \"Sudo Guard\", \"sudo rm /tmp/test_50_del/f29.txt\", \"f29.txt\")\n\n# --- Category 4: Alternative Unix Utilities (Bypasses) ---\nadd_test(30, \"shred -u (secure delete)\", \"Unix Utility\", \"shred -u /tmp/test_50_del/f30.txt\", \"f30.txt\")\nadd_test(31, \"shred -z -u -n 1\", \"Unix Utility\", \"shred -z -u -n 1 /tmp/test_50_del/f31.txt\", \"f31.txt\")\nadd_test(32, \"dd if=/dev/null of=...\", \"Block Overwrite\", \"dd if=/dev/null of=/tmp/test_50_del/f32.txt\", \"f32.txt\")\nadd_test(33, \"cp /dev/null ...\", \"File Overwrite\", \"cp /dev/null /tmp/test_50_del/f33.txt\", \"f33.txt\")\nadd_test(34, \"tee < /dev/null\", \"Pipe Truncate\", \"tee /tmp/test_50_del/f34.txt < /dev/null\", \"f34.txt\")\nadd_test(35, \"cat /dev/null > ...\", \"Redirection Wipe\", \"cat /dev/null > /tmp/test_50_del/f35.txt\", \"f35.txt\")\nadd_test(36, \"sed -i 'd' ...\", \"Stream Wipe\", \"sed -i 'd' /tmp/test_50_del/f36.txt\", \"f36.txt\")\nadd_test(37, \"tar --remove-files\", \"Archive Removal\", \"tar -czf /tmp/test_50_del/f37.tar.gz --remove-files -C /tmp/test_50_del f37.txt\", \"f37.txt\")\nadd_test(38, \"bzip2 (deletes source)\", \"Compress Deletion\", \"bzip2 /tmp/test_50_del/f38.txt\", \"f38.txt\")\nadd_test(39, \"gzip (deletes source)\", \"Compress Deletion\", \"gzip /tmp/test_50_del/f39.txt\", \"f39.txt\")\nadd_test(40, \"head -c 0 > ...\", \"Truncate Redir\", \"head -c 0 /dev/zero > /tmp/test_50_del/f40.txt\", \"f40.txt\")\n\n# --- Category 5: Scripting Interpreters & Syscalls (Bypasses) ---\nadd_test(41, \"Perl unlink()\", \"Perl Interpreter\", \"perl -e \\\"unlink('/tmp/test_50_del/f41.txt')\\\"\", \"f41.txt\")\nadd_test(42, \"Direct Syscall 87 (unlink)\", \"Kernel Syscall\", \"python3 -c \\\"import ctypes; ctypes.CDLL(None).syscall(87, b'/tmp/test_50_del/f42.txt')\\\"\", \"f42.txt\")\nadd_test(43, \"Direct Syscall 263 (unlinkat)\", \"Kernel Syscall\", \"python3 -c \\\"import ctypes; ctypes.CDLL(None).syscall(263, -100, b'/tmp/test_50_del/f43.txt', 0)\\\"\", \"f43.txt\")\nadd_test(44, \"Python getattr(os, 'unlink')\", \"Dynamic Python\", \"python3 -c \\\"getattr(__import__('os'), 'un' + 'link')('/tmp/test_50_del/f44.txt')\\\"\", \"f44.txt\")\nadd_test(45, \"Python open(..., 'w').close()\", \"Python Truncate\", \"python3 -c \\\"open('/tmp/test_50_del/f45.txt', 'w').close()\\\"\", \"f45.txt\")\nadd_test(46, \"Python f.truncate(0)\", \"Python Truncate\", \"python3 -c \\\"f=open('/tmp/test_50_del/f46.txt', 'r+'); f.truncate(0); f.close()\\\"\", \"f46.txt\")\nadd_test(47, \"Base64 Obfuscated rm\", \"Shell Obfuscation\", \"echo 'cm0gL3RtcC90ZXN0XzUwX2RlbC9mNDcudHh0' | base64 -d | sh\", \"f47.txt\")\nadd_test(48, \"Hex Escaped rm\", \"Shell Obfuscation\", \"printf '\\\\x72\\\\x6d\\\\x20%s\\\\n' /tmp/test_50_del/f48.txt | sh\", \"f48.txt\")\nadd_test(49, \"Dynamic os.system string split\", \"Dynamic Shell\", \"python3 -c \\\"import os; os.system('echo f49 > /dev/null; /bin/' + 'r' + 'm /tmp/test_50_del/f49.txt')\\\"\", \"f49.txt\")\nadd_test(50, \"Compiled C binary unlink()\", \"Compiled Binary\", \"/tmp/test_50_del/c_unlink_del\", \"f50.txt\")\n\n# Setup C binary for test 50\nc_code = \"\"\"\n#include <unistd.h>\nint main() {\n    unlink(\"/tmp/test_50_del/f50.txt\");\n    return 0;\n}\n\"\"\"\nwith open(\"/tmp/test_50_del/c_del.c\", \"w\") as f:\n    f.write(c_code)\nsubprocess.run([\"gcc\", \"-O2\", \"/tmp/test_50_del/c_del.c\", \"-o\", \"/tmp/test_50_del/c_unlink_del\"], check=True)\n\n# Run the Benchmark\nresults = []\nblocked_count = 0\ndeleted_count = 0\ntruncated_count = 0\nintact_count = 0\n\nprint(\"=\" * 80)\nprint(f\"RUNNING 50-COMMAND DELETION BENCHMARK AUDIT\")\nprint(\"=\" * 80)\n\nfor t in tests:\n    target = t[\"target\"]\n    # Setup target\n    if t[\"is_dir\"]:\n        shutil.rmtree(target, ignore_errors=True)\n        os.makedirs(target, exist_ok=True)\n    else:\n        with open(target, \"w\") as f:\n            f.write(\"INITIAL_DATA_CONTENT_12345\\n\" * 10)\n    \n    initial_exists = os.path.exists(target)\n    initial_size = os.path.getsize(target) if (initial_exists and not t[\"is_dir\"]) else 0\n\n    # Step 1: Evaluate delete_guard.py PreToolUse decision\n    is_dest, reason, rule_id = inspect_command(t[\"cmd\"])\n    guard_decision = \"BLOCKED\" if is_dest else \"ALLOWED\"\n\n    # Step 2: Execute command only if ALLOWED by guard (or simulate hook pass-through)\n    exec_status = \"SKIPPED (HOOK BLOCKED)\"\n    actual_deleted = False\n    actual_truncated = False\n\n    if guard_decision == \"BLOCKED\":\n        blocked_count += 1\n        final_exists = os.path.exists(target)\n        final_size = os.path.getsize(target) if (final_exists and not t[\"is_dir\"]) else 0\n        status_label = \"🛡️ BLOCKED BY GUARD\"\n    else:\n        # Guard ALLOWED this command — let's execute in shell!\n        try:\n            res = subprocess.run(t[\"cmd\"], shell=True, capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=5)\n            final_exists = os.path.exists(target)\n            if not final_exists:\n                actual_deleted = True\n                deleted_count += 1\n                status_label = \"💥 DELETED (BYPASS!)\"\n            else:\n                final_size = os.path.getsize(target) if not t[\"is_dir\"] else 0\n                if final_size == 0 and initial_size > 0:\n                    actual_truncated = True\n                    truncated_count += 1\n                    status_label = \"⚠️ TRUNCATED (DATA WIPED)\"\n                else:\n                    intact_count += 1\n                    status_label = \"🔒 INTACT\"\n        except Exception as e:\n            status_label = f\"ERROR ({e})\"\n\n    results.append({\n        \"id\": t[\"id\"],\n        \"name\": t[\"name\"],\n        \"category\": t[\"category\"],\n        \"cmd\": t[\"cmd\"],\n        \"guard\": guard_decision,\n        \"rule\": rule_id if is_dest else \"-\",\n        \"status\": status_label\n    })\n\n    print(f\"[{t['id']:02d}/50] {t['name']:<32} | Guard: {guard_decision:<7} | Outcome: {status_label}\")\n\nprint(\"=\" * 80)\nprint(f\"BENCHMARK SUMMARY:\")\nprint(f\"Total Commands Tested : 50\")\nprint(f\"Blocked by Hook Guard : {blocked_count} / 50\")\nprint(f\"Bypassed & Deleted    : {deleted_count} / 50\")\nprint(f\"Bypassed & Truncated  : {truncated_count} / 50\")\nprint(f\"Bypassed but Intact   : {intact_count} / 50\")\nprint(\"=\" * 80)\n\n# Write results to Markdown report\nreport_path = \"/home/azureuser/AGY-MASTER/REPORTS/BENCHMARK_50_DELETION_COMMANDS.md\"\nwith open(report_path, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n    f.write(\"# 50-COMMAND DELETION BENCHMARK AUDIT REPORT\\n\\n\")\n    f.write(f\"Target Host: Azure VM 'FatehAli'  \\n\")\n    f.write(f\"Date: 2026-09-26  \\n\\n\")\n    f.write(\"## Summary Statistics\\n\\n\")\n    f.write(f\"- **Total Tests:** 50\\n\")\n    f.write(f\"- **🛡️ Blocked by delete_guard.py:** {blocked_count} (Guardrail held)\\n\")\n    f.write(f\"- **💥 Successfully Deleted:** {deleted_count} (Bypassed guardrail & deleted by OS)\\n\")\n    f.write(f\"- **⚠️ Successfully Truncated (0 bytes):** {truncated_count} (Bypassed guardrail & wiped file content)\\n\")\n    f.write(f\"- **🔒 Intact:** {intact_count}\\n\\n\")\n    f.write(\"## Granular Results Table\\n\\n\")\n    f.write(\"| ID | Command / Technique | Category | Hook Decision | Rule ID | Live Outcome |\\n\")\n    f.write(\"| :---: | :--- | :--- | :---: | :--- | :---: |\\n\")\n    for r in results:\n        f.write(f\"| {r['id']:02d} | `{r['cmd']}` | {r['category']} | {r['guard']} | `{r['rule']}` | {r['status']} |\\n\")\n\nprint(f\"Detailed Markdown report saved to: {report_path}\")\n","Description":"Benchmark script to execute 50 distinct deletion commands against delete_guard and kernel","Overwrite":true,"TargetFile":"/home/azureuser/benchmark_50_delete_tests.py","toolAction":"Creating 50-command benchmark script","toolSummary":"Create benchmark script"}}]}
